\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Profiler-in-the-loop GPU optimization is effective, but it assumes repeated access to the target accelerator. We study whether off-the-shelf LLMs can classify a kernel's bandwidth-bound versus compute-bound Roofline regime earlier in that loop, from software artifacts alone, before runtime profiling is available.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
